    "note": "If the gradient is a cosmological field its direction stays fixed on the CMB axis (deg_from_cmb_axis ~ const, small); if it is a solar-radiation-pressure orbit error it moves with the Sun (deg_from_sun_axis ~ const, small).  Over this ~6-week baseline the two candidate directions are only ~30-40 deg apart, so they are not cleanly separable; a full-year baseline (Sun sweeps 360 deg, CMB axis fixed) would be decisive."
